# libcss: the CSS mask properties, read as background ones
# Generated 2026-09-24
#
# libcss has no masking. Sites use mask-image for monochrome icons -- a span
# with a background-color, shaped by an SVG mask -- so each such icon drew
# as a solid block of its colour (Wikipedia's Minerva and Vector skins: the
# Language / Watch / Edit bars). A real mask property would mean new
# computed-style fields in files MacSurf hand-edited after generation; this
# maps the mask properties onto the background ones at parse time instead:
#   mask-image, -webkit-mask-image         -> background-image, and
#                                             background-color: transparent
#                                             (unless the value is none)
#   mask-size / -position / -repeat (+ -webkit-) -> background-*
#   mask, -webkit-mask                     -> the background shorthand
# so the icon shows its own shape, in the SVG's own colour rather than the
# element's. One lookup, css__property_id(), serves both the parser and the
# deferred var() path (custom_properties.c), which re-parses by name at
# cascade time (Minerva's mask-size is calc(var(...) + 4px)).
# Limits: an element with both a background image and a mask shows only
# the mask image; libcss's background shorthand does not take "/ size", so
# -webkit-mask with a size is dropped.
# See docs/phase-0/11-real-sites.md.

